<title>SINGAPORE: Comfort half yr net up 23.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Comfort half yr net up 23.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				 16.01   vs   13.00</p>
<p>    Group shares (cents)		    3.00  vs     2.70</p>
<p>    Turnover				   107.44  vs   77.42</p>
<p>    Interest and other income		2.00  vs    1.08</p>
<p>    Profit before tax			 23.47  vs   18.55</p>
<p>    Tax					    6.84  vs    5.34</p>
<p>Note - Taxi operator Comfort Group Ltd said the rise in its pre-tax profit was largely due to its expanded taxi operations and a change in the method of depreciating its taxi fleet. It said it expects its results for the current financial year to be better.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
